So, to use a reference some of you might get, a town similar to Karakura in
the show Bleach, yes?

On Mon, Jul 12, 2010 at 3:47 PM, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:

> > I understood that, but the map of the city should be consistent with the
> map
> > of the country. How big is the city (inhabitants, and kilometers)?
>
> About 5x5km set on a grid with some houses set out a good 5-10 minutes
> walking distance from the grid.
> Population? About 5-10k. Enough to support a metropolitan-esque town,
> but nothing huge.
>
> I forsee cars being something rarely used, so roads should look more
> like they're built for bicycles, and there should be a train/rail
> system that runs from this town to Bertcad and other areas in short
> amounts of time. Perhaps in Bertcad they're used a bit more, but I
> don't forsee them being a necessity as Bertcad probably has a very
> efficient public transportation system.
>
> Harl!
>
> So... Yeah.
>
> Vocab List:
>
> prenu
> pendo
> skami
> plise
> perli
> gerku
> mlatu
> cipni
> smacu
> ractu
> zutse
> sanli
> bajra
> dansu
>
> Is this enough for one episode? I start with objects, then moved to
> actions which could be easily demonstrated in animation.
>
> Also, I'm starting to think that backgrounds will be easier if we
> model locations in 3D and cell-shade them, or at least rotoscope the
> entire scene to fit the animation style. This is just a thought, but
> it would keep locations consistent (if that's important at all).
>
> The script seems to be coming along nicely. We need the airport
> portion fleshed out a little more, but after that I think the first
> episode has been rough-drafted enough.
